# Backup age recipient (public key — safe to track in version control).
#
# Age recipients are public keys: they are designed to be shared, since only
# the matching PRIVATE key (identity file) can decrypt anything encrypted to
# them. Tracking a public key in git is not a leak.
#
# That said, the line below is a PLACEHOLDER, not a real, live recipient.
# Generate your own keypair and replace it before using these scripts:
#
#   age-keygen -o age-key.txt      # writes a new "AGE-SECRET-KEY-1..." identity
#                                   # to age-key.txt and prints the matching
#                                   # "age1..." public recipient to stderr
#   age-keygen -y age-key.txt       # re-derive just the public recipient later
#
# Then:
#   1. Replace the age1... line below with YOUR public recipient.
#   2. Store age-key.txt's contents (the private identity) in macOS Keychain —
#      never commit it. See SETUP.md in this directory.
#
# EXAMPLE PLACEHOLDER RECIPIENT — replace with your own `age-keygen -y` output:
age1qyqszqgpqyqszqgpqyqszqgpqyqszqgpqyqszqgpqyqszqgpqyqszqgpqgpqyqs
